BEGIN_DESC
AtmoFX: a Delta Glider enters Jupiter's atmosphere (needs the AtmoFX fork of D3D9Client). At start the AtmoFX probe puts the glider 1000 km above the reference radius, 600 km west of a sunlit point (sun ~35 deg), flying east at 4 km/s relative to the air, 5 deg below the horizon, nose along the flow. Orbiter's own physics does the rest: the air thickens over 700-500 km - through the haze and the ammonia deck - and brakes the glider hard (Orbiter does not destroy it).
External view behind the glider (F1 - cockpit). Time acceleration speeds it up. The invisible probe only places the glider; its status line stays on screen.
END_DESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 60970.5
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship JDG
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET JDG
  MODE Extern
  POS 3.00 -170.00 12.00
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 60.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_HUD
  TYPE Surface
END_HUD

BEGIN_SHIPS
Probe:AtmoProbe
  STATUS Landed Jupiter
  POS 0.0000000 -15.0000000
  HEADING 0.00
  ALTKM 455
  SUNELEV 35
  CLOUDS 0
  LAUNCH JDG 1000 4 5 600
END
JDG:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Landed Jupiter
  POS 0.0000000 -15.0000000
  HEADING 90.00
  RCSMODE 0
  AFCMODE 7
  PRPLEVEL 0:1.000000 1:1.000000
  NAVFREQ 0 0 0 0
END
END_SHIPS
